==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*2 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[Maawth]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Dark Emperor Santa]] spawns as the boss.
**3 [[Maawth]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
**3 [[Ursamajor]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
**3 [[LeMurr]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
**1 [[Satan Claus]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
**4 [[One Horn]]s spawn, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
**5 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Due to the strength of the [[:Category:Unstarred Alien Enemies|Alien]] enemies here, beating this stage is not feasible without ''all'' of the [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] from [[Into the Future]].

While the potential drop of a Yellow Behemoth Stone might seem enticing, beating the stage fast enough to actually obtain it is unlikely, especially without very specific Uber Rares. Using a [[Battle Items#Rich Cat|Rich Cat]] can help remove the need to stall for money, leading to a faster overall time.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Ancient Egg: N202 (Special Cat)|Armored Firefly Cat]] - While admittedly a strange choice at first glance, at Lv.30+20 (or Lv.40+10/Lv.50) they have 20,250 health, which is enough to survive at least one hit from every enemy except Dark Emperor Santa. Plus, they target both [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] and Aliens, and them getting a weaken off is decently likely thanks to their low cost and spammability.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] - Unsurprisingly, Courier makes for a strong option for this stage thanks to his excellent damage against Red and Long Distance letting him snipe Dark Emperor Santa. Do be wary about using him near the beginning, however, as he can accidentally trigger the boss wave too early.
*[[Ancient Egg: N105 (Rare Cat)|Racquet Cat]] - She has good range, Area Attack and piercing range, all of which combine to make her an excellent crowd-controller for this stage. She can use the Sir Seals and One Horns as stepping stones to hit the Alien backliners. Since the Aliens being knocked back gives them less chances to attack, she also has good synergy with Roe Cat, who struggles with being hit by the Aliens.
*[[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]]/[[Ancient Egg: N108 (Super Rare Cat)|Soap Cat]] - Both are tankers, but both only target one of the two traits in this stage, leaving them pretty vulnerable against the other. Using both wastes money and valuable slots, so only one of the two is recommended. Aliens are the more prominent trait here, and Soap Cat has one less knockback which makes them the better overall choice, but they're also harder to obtain than Roe Cat is.
*[[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] - Housewife is a staple in any stage with threatening backliners. When Talented with Savage Blow, she can take advantage of her piercing range to wipe out the Maawths and Ursamajors and deal huge damage to Satan Claus.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] - Is able to pick off the Sir Seals and One Horns for extra cash and deal decent chip damage to the remaining enemies.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Machine]] - Cat Machine is a tanker that targets both Red and Alien enemies, naturally making them a great choice for this stage. Beware that they are rather vulnerable to Satan Claus' Warp, and the LeMurrs can shred through their health with ease if left unchecked.
*[[Terun (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Terun]] - Has immunity to both Freeze and Weaken, on top of outranging every enemy here except Dark Emperor Santa. Her slow also has really good uptime, which helps nullify the pushing power of the enemies. She ''can'' work pre-[[True Form]], but the stats boost provided by Strong makes her significantly more useful here.
*[[Sharpshooter Saki (Uber Rare Cat)|Sharpshooter Saki]] - Her first form targets exclusively Red and Aliens, which are the sole enemy types found in this stage. This, combined with her ludicrous Long Distance and decent speed, makes her an excellent pick for this stage.
*[[Winter General Kaihime (Uber Rare Cat)|Winter Commander Kaihime]] - Fairly similar to Terun, except she slows Floating instead of Alien and her combination of [[Surge Attack]] and [[Savage Blow]] lets her snipe the backliners better than Terun can. She also has notably higher average DPS than Terun, at least before Terun's True Form.

